Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: accelerate YUV arithmetic and cache exact NV12 terms

Use portable bit scans for YUV fixed-point multiplication and precompute
8-bit NV12 channel contributions once before device registration. Keep
existing scaling, truncation, rounding, matrices and rotated chroma siting.
Dispatch XRGB8888 writeback once per row instead of indirectly per pixel.
Copy opaque pixels and skip zero transparent pixels with identical blending
semantics; retain the original equation for every other alpha/color value.
Tables occupy 108 KiB across six encoding/range pairs and become read-only
after module init. Other pixel formats retain their existing readers.
Baseline: Linux stable v7.3.3. Local experimental patch, not upstreamed.

